WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.820
Let's try the D-slider.

2
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.570
This device only works from left to right.

3
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.340
Its purpose is to drop stitches

4
00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:12.620
from the main bed while maintaining the
needle positions of the needles in work.

5
00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.540
It's used for the drop
stitch lace technique

6
00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:20.940
using the ribber. With no yarn
in the needles, manually put a few needles

7
00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:28.100
into B or working position and a few
needles into D or middle position.

8
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:33.340
Position the D-slider left of the needles
in work on the needle bed.

9
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:38.020
Pass it from left to right,
pressing down slightly.

10
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:41.180
Notice how the needles engage.

11
00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:46.300
Also notice that the needles will
remain in their original position.

12
00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:51.980
If there were stitches in work, all of
the stitches would drop off the needles.

13
00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:57.260
Now, if you are going to be working short
rows or you have needles in E position or

14
00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:02.020
hold position, they will also
engage with the D-slider.

15
00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:06.980
If you want to work short rows with this
device, manually knit the held stitches

16
00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:12.380
with Ravel cord and position
the needles back to A position.

17
00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.260
When you're done with the transfers,

18
00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:18.130
pick up the D-slider,
remove it and set it aside.

19
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.720
It only works from left to right.

